      "The project quickly went beyond school boundaries, fostering environmental discussions integrated into the curriculum and engaging families and communities. Children began collecting bottle caps in streets and parks, while schools expanded the campaign by setting up collection points in public buildings, bars, and restaurants. The project’s reach grew exponentially, supported by mobilization activities at cooperative events and communication campaigns that reinforce environmental awareness. More than 500 kilograms of bottle caps were collected during the project’s first three months. The aim is to reach 2 tons by the end of 2025. The initiative generates resources for the schools and fosters lasting cultural change, encouraging sustainable practices in the region. For 2026, Cresol Evolução plans to expand the campaign to all interested schools within the cooperative’s area of operation and to establish partnerships with other organizations, consolidating the project as a regional benchmark in environmental education and circular economy.",
